  "description": "The Nua Kensho Single Speed is a modern titanium commuter designed around efficiency, comfort, and long-term reliability. Built for daily urban riding, it combines minimalist single-speed simplicity with carefully chosen materials and components that enhance ride quality without compromise. At its core, Kensho Single Speed is crafted from Grade 9 titanium, a material prized for its exceptional strength-to-weight ratio and natural vibration damping. This gives the bike a lively yet comfortable feel, smoothing rough pavement and reducing fatigue on longer commutes. The dropped seatstays further contribute to shock absorption, subtly filtering road buzz while preserving a responsive, direct ride. Up front, the Kensho is paired with the Nua Commuter carbon fork. Its tapered 1.5″ steerer delivers a noticeably stiffer front end, improving steering precision, braking control, and stability when accelerating hard or navigating traffic. The carbon construction keeps weight low while helping absorb high-frequency vibrations from the road. The build is completed with a Campagnolo Zonda GT wheelset, chosen for its blend of durability and confidence-inspiring handling. Designed to perform across rough city streets and even mixed surfaces, the Zonda GT wheels accelerate efficiently, hold speed well, and add a refined, performance-oriented feel to the bike. Available as a frameset or complete bicycle, the Nua Kensho Single Speed is built to order and designed to be a long-term companion for urban riders who value simplicity, quality, and a smooth, fast commute.",
